  {
   "key": "scene_06",
   "text": "Pedri is the name the numbers pick out. FotMob rates him 9.0, the highest on the pitch, with 6 chances created. FotMob has no running data for La Liga games, so look at the ball: 107 touches and 10 recoveries, his most in his last 6 games. And Fermín López, who gave the ball away for the first goal: 4 goals in his last 4 games, one of them tonight, in 68 minutes on the pitch. Flick put it simply after the match: \"If we play like this, the opponent gets tired.\" Barça had 70 percent of the ball, and 10 corners to Villarreal's none.",
