  {
   "key": "scene_07",
   "text": "Expected goals, or xG, is learned from past shots: distance, angle, foot or head. It says how often a chance like it is scored. FotMob supplies the numbers. Villarreal's two goals were worth 0.04 and 0.06 xG. Almost nothing. Barça's penalty at minute 23 was worth 0.79, and it hit the post. Over the night, Barça finish on 3.29 xG to Villarreal's 0.17. 93 percent of it came through the centre, and many of those shots were blocked. Replay these chances 20,000 times, and Barça win 97 in 100. So the 0-2 half did lie. Barça's chances were not the problem. Luck and finishing were.",
   "url": "https://media.viewmax.io/users/7RRunw8K5Hq1WuIqMTzGxHdTQZ5z8lPX/voiceover/4b1a0f4b-ee44-4f8f-aa1a-621aede3b0f8.wav",
