  {
   "key": "scene_09",
   "text": "So, was De Jong the weak point? Khel Now says he was caught out of position for the second goal, leaving Eric García to chase Oluwaseyi. Pedri calls him \"extraordinary\". FotMob's numbers lean his way: 104 of 110 passes, 7 recoveries, 3 of 3 ground duels won, never dribbled past. They cannot show where he stood when that pass was played. Barça were unlucky at one end, shaky at the other, and still won 3-2. Two questions for you. Was De Jong at centre-back a risk worth taking? And was Fermín's red card fair? Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next match.",
